@@ -0,0 +1,13 @@
+# Selected CSV input through normal saved solutions
+
+This increment pairs with Portal branch `codex/normal-designer-run-20261118`, based on its published `72e440c` checkpoint. WP3 starts from published `7e16c81`. It is development source, not an installed runtime or a new real-DGAN qualification.
+
+The normal Portal compiler can send a small designer-selected CSV as an existing `inline` / `csv` DataReference. The configured Portuguese training connector now decodes those bytes under its existing operator input-byte ceiling, records their hash and submits them as the source API's multipart CSV. It does not interpret the data as settings, a path or a remote URL. Its file/approved-origin modes remain available. Node-specific scientific data/index requirements still belong to the provider.
+
+The connector advertises `input_transports: ["inline-csv-v1"]` for its implemented training operation. This is runtime capability metadata; it does not alter the provider's versioned parameter definitions. Other compatible services may advertise the same transport without Portal service-ID branches. They must actually implement its bounded base64 CSV handling.
+
+WP3 advertises `input_transport_validation: "wrapper-input-v1"`. Read-only compatibility and workflow submission verify selected CSV support on every graph start operation before creating tasks or worker state. The Control client checks the same capability before dispatch. An older runtime or wrapper without the declaration rejects this new input path. JSON and existing legacy requests retain their current path. The graph still receives one initial input across its start operations; independently selected per-step datasets and larger managed datasets remain future work.
+
+Source verification: the Portuguese API test executes the unchanged FastAPI source with an explicit DGAN dependency double. The shared Danish tests execute their real enumerator/renderer. The paired Portal test additionally uses normal provider/admin/designer API routes, real HTTP WP3/Redis/Worker/Control, saved CSV selection and owned HTTP result ingestion. Assistant mode substitutes the assistant provider response. These establish integration boundaries, not actual DGAN/browser/partner acceptance.
+
+The previous Windows real-DGAN evidence remains historical qualification of its exact inspected tree/image. This increment must be installed separately in a new development execution workspace, preserving the retained demo, review-only workspace, existing journals, models and closed grants. No paid call or production deployment is included.
